From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000105 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rob Vogelaar <rob.vogelaar@libertyglobal.com>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 14:26:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] agent: serialize WSC M2 and retry failed subdoc delivery

A four-extender cold reconstruction reproduced two related tri-band races on
the third extender. The 2.4 and 6 GHz M2 frames entered
handle_autoconfig_wsc_m2 concurrently. Ten WSC TLVs authenticated, but only
one invocation reached encrypted-settings processing. The successful
invocation then queued a OneWifi SOUTH subdoc and moved the radio out of
wsc_m2_pending before delivery was confirmed. When the synchronous RBUS set
lost its provider response, the radio remained in owconfig_pending forever and
the existing lost-M2 retry could not run.

Serialize M2 parsing across the agent because its WSC crypto/settings path is
not re-entrant across radio service threads. If the bounded OneWifi subdoc set
fails, put the affected radio back in wsc_m2_pending. The existing bounded,
fresh-crypto M1 retry then replays only that radio's idempotent configuration.
Successful sets and callbacks retain the normal state machine.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 src/agent/em_agent.cpp             | 22 ++++++++++++++++++----
 src/em/config/em_configuration.cpp |  6 ++++++
 2 files changed, 24 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/agent/em_agent.cpp b/src/agent/em_agent.cpp
index 1111111..2222222 100644
--- a/src/agent/em_agent.cpp
+++ b/src/agent/em_agent.cpp
@@ -293,14 +293,29 @@ void em_agent_t::handle_m2ctrl_configuration(em_bus_event_t *evt)
 {
-    unsigned int num;
+    int result;
     wifi_bus_desc_t *desc;
 
     if((desc = get_bus_descriptor()) == NULL) {
        printf("descriptor is null");
+       return;
     }
 
     if (m_orch->is_cmd_type_in_progress(evt) == true) {
         m_agent_cmd->send_result(em_cmd_out_status_prev_cmd_in_progress);
-    } else if ((num = static_cast<unsigned int>(m_data_model.analyze_m2ctrl_configuration(evt, desc, &m_bus_hdl))) == 0) {
+        return;
+    }
+
+    result = m_data_model.analyze_m2ctrl_configuration(evt, desc, &m_bus_hdl);
+    if (result < 0) {
+        m2ctrl_radioconfig *config =
+            reinterpret_cast<m2ctrl_radioconfig *>(evt->u.raw_buff);
+        std::string ruid = util::mac_to_string(config->radio_mac[0]);
+        em_t *em = static_cast<em_t *>(hash_map_get(m_em_map, ruid.c_str()));
+        if (em != NULL && em->get_state() == em_state_agent_owconfig_pending) {
+            em->set_state(em_state_agent_wsc_m2_pending);
+            em_printfout("OneWifi subdoc delivery failed for radio %s; re-arming WSC M2 recovery",
+                ruid.c_str());
+        }
+    } else if (result == 0) {
 	    printf("analyze_onewifi_private_subdoc complete");
     }
 }
diff --git a/src/em/config/em_configuration.cpp b/src/em/config/em_configuration.cpp
index 3333333..4444444 100644
--- a/src/em/config/em_configuration.cpp
+++ b/src/em/config/em_configuration.cpp
@@ -4865,5 +4865,11 @@ int em_configuration_t::handle_autoconfig_wsc_m2(unsigned char *buff, unsigned
 int em_configuration_t::handle_autoconfig_wsc_m2(unsigned char *buff, unsigned int len)
 {
+    // Radio service threads can deliver tri-band M2 frames concurrently. The
+    // enrollee crypto/settings path is stateful and is not re-entrant across
+    // those invocations, so serialize it through subdoc creation.
+    static std::mutex wsc_m2_mutex;
+    std::lock_guard<std::mutex> lock(wsc_m2_mutex);
+
     em_tlv_t *tlv;
     int tmp_len;
     unsigned int wsc_tlv_count = 0;
